      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:1:12:1",
      "text": [
        " فِي الْمَرْأَةِ الْحَامِلِ تَأْكُلُ السَّفَرْجَلَ فَإِنَّ الْوَلَدَ يَكُونُ أَطْيَبَ رِيحاً وَ أَصْفَى لَوْناً ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from salma Bin Al Khattab, from Usman Bin Abdul Rahman, from Shurhabeel Bin Muslim, ",
          "‘He<sup>asws</sup> said regarding the pregnant woman: ‘She should eat the quince, so the child would happen to be of pleasant aroma, and clear colour’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "1. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Salmah ibn al-Khattab from ‘Uthman ibn ‘Abd al- Rahman from Sharahbil ibn Muslim who has said the following: “He (the Imam), ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘A pregnant woman should eat quince because the child grows up of fine smell and clear color.’” "
        ]
      }
